ready: 1
kind: journey
id: capture.remember
display_id: FLOW-CAPTURE-REMEMBER
module: capture
actors: [actor.agent, actor.owner]
title: Remember something on purpose
summary: The agent or the owner captures something worth keeping, or the owner imports memories from a file or an earlier release.
trigger: Something happened that is worth keeping, or the owner has memories elsewhere
steps:
  - capture.remember.decide
  - capture.remember.agent-call
  - capture.remember.agent-result
  - capture.remember.held
  - capture.remember.unavailable
  - capture.remember.owner-command
  - capture.remember.owner-result
sequences:
  - capture.seq.raw
  - memory.seq.write
  - capture.seq.import
  - capture.seq.legacy-import
related:
  - to: consolidation.review
    label: Held memories wait in review
    relation: leads_to
rationale: >-
  Most experience is captured from transcripts without any call. This journey covers the times
  the agent or the owner chooses what to keep, and the result says plainly whether it was stored,
  repeated, or held, so the agent never claims a memory that was not kept.
